# 基本図形編集の描画の速さを、同じ実行の中で比べる (design 11.3), for tools/ui_run.py:
# a figure of 2000 small rectangles and two zigzag lines (mkbig) opened by the desktop's
# figure editor (open) and by the figure editor running as a process (pfig) in turn, three
# times each, so that both are measured under the same load of the machine. Each time a
# rectangle is taken and then the empty page pressed, five times: each press changes what
# is taken. Compared: "desktop: figure input to screen US us" and "figure: input to screen
# US us" (from the press, as the pointer told it, to the window drawn), and the times of the
# drawing ("desktop: figure drew in", "figure: drew part ... in").
# the desktop's figure editor opened by open, whatever the program object says (figproc kernel)
figproc kernel
mkbig fig 2000 200
# round 1
logmark
open big
waitwin 画用紙 600
sync 600
wait 800
click 123 152
sync 600
wait 300
click 600 600
sync 600
wait 300
click 135 152
sync 600
wait 300
click 600 600
sync 600
wait 300
click 147 152
sync 600
wait 300
click 600 600
sync 600
wait 300
click 159 152
sync 600
wait 300
click 600 600
sync 600
wait 300
click 171 152
sync 600
wait 300
click 600 600
sync 600
wait 300
key 08 01
sync 600
wait 500
logmark
pfig big
expectsincein 60 figure: opened
wait 800
logmark
click 123 152
expectsince figure: input to screen
wait 300
logmark
click 600 600
expectsince figure: input to screen
wait 300
logmark
